# -*- text -*-
#
# Prisma Routing's RADIUS attributes (#607): vendor 67033, the product's own
# IANA Private Enterprise Number (assigned 2026-10-02, #554; the SNMP MIB is
# under the same number). Install it on the RADIUS server beside its other
# dictionaries - FreeRADIUS: copy it to /usr/share/freeradius/ and add
# `$INCLUDE dictionary.prisma` to /etc/freeradius/3.0/dictionary. The box
# prints this file with `show aaa radius dictionary`.
#
# Rates are kbit/s, an integer: 20000 is 20 Mbit/s. 0, or the attribute
# absent, is no limit in that direction. In an Access-Accept they are the
# session's plan; in a CoA-Request, a new plan for the live session.
#
# THE NUMBER PLAN. Each range is kept for one kind of attribute, so a later
# attribute lands beside its kind and no number is ever reused:
#     1-15   subscriber rate and QoS
#    16-31   addressing (pools, IPv6 delegation)
#    32-47   CGNAT (BPA pool selection, port blocks)
#    48-63   session control
#    64-255  unassigned
# An attribute, once shipped, keeps its number and its type for ever.
#
VENDOR		Prisma				67033

BEGIN-VENDOR	Prisma

# The session's download (box to subscriber) and upload (subscriber to box)
# limit, kbit/s. A VPP policer on the session interface's output and input.
ATTRIBUTE	Prisma-Rate-Limit-Down			1	integer
ATTRIBUTE	Prisma-Rate-Limit-Up			2	integer

END-VENDOR	Prisma
